{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion capabilities and sensor outcomes. The specification automata enforce conservative exploration: random_walk is used for exploration in clear states, move_forward is only allowed in a dedicated commit state after confirming a clear path, and all obstacle events force immediate turn-based recovery. Obstacle recovery states only allow a single safe turn action, and no forward or random_walk actions are enabled in any obstacle state. The design ensures deterministic, non-stalling, and conservative collision avoidance.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion commands and sensor outcomes to modularize perception and actuation.",
    "Specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe actions, enforce conservative recovery from obstacles, and alternate between random_walk and short forward progress for steady exploration."
  ],
